{
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Electricity rates by state (EIA Table 5.6.A)",
    "description": "Average retail electricity prices in cents per kilowatthour for the 50 states, the District of Columbia and the U.S. total, from the U.S. Energy Information Administration's Electric Power Monthly Table 5.6.A: residential, commercial and industrial prices for August 2026 and for August 2025, the same month a year earlier. Each row says which month it is and whether EIA treats that year as final or preliminary. EIA's note: Values for 2025 are final. Values for 2026 are preliminary estimates based on a cutoff model sample. A price that EIA does not print (it shows \"--\" or \"NM\") is empty. A state average is not a utility rate: the price on your own bill depends on your utility and plan.",
    "url": "https://fedratecalc.com/data/electricity-rates-by-state/",
    "license": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",
    "licenseName": "CC BY 4.0",
    "attribution": "FedRateCalc",
    "attributionText": "FedRateCalc (https://fedratecalc.com/data/electricity-rates-by-state/), CC BY 4.0",
    "notes": [
      "Values for 2025 are final. Values for 2026 are preliminary estimates based on a cutoff model sample."
    ],
    "sources": [
